2025-05-01 02:20:32 - Thread-807 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Below is a short “column‑mapping / condition” cheat‑sheet followed by ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (simple → complex → almost‑final).  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes as required.

==================================================
POSSIBLY RELEVANT COLUMNS
--------------------------------------------------
"Modality"               : filter to ‘SEG’, ‘RTSTRUCT’  
"SOPClassUID"            : filter to ‘1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4’ (SEG storage)  
"ReferencedSeriesSequence",
"ReferencedImageSequence",
"SourceImageSequence",
"SourceImageEvidenceSequence",
"StudiesContainingOtherReferencedInstancesSequence"  
                         : must be NULL / empty when we want “no references”  
"collection_name"        : collection identifier for final grouping  
"StudyInstanceUID"       : study identifier (needed for viewer URL)  
"SeriesInstanceUID"      : series identifier (one level under study)  
"instance_size"          : byte size of the individual object  
==================================================

TEN STEPWISE QUERIES
(The LIMIT 20 keeps them light; remove it when you really run the final one.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick glance at modalities present in this release
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect different SOP Class UIDs encountered in SEG / RTSTRUCT objects
SELECT DISTINCT "SOPClassUID"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "Modality" IN ('SEG','RTSTRUCT')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: How many rows have no referenced series or images?
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "no_ref_candidate_rows"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "ReferencedSeriesSequence"        IS NULL
  AND  "ReferencedImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND  "SourceImageSequence"             IS NULL
  AND  "SourceImageEvidenceSequence"     IS NULL;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Peek at a few SEG objects that already satisfy the “no reference” requirement
SELECT  "SOPInstanceUID",
        "Modality",
        "SOPClassUID",
        "instance_size"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "Modality"      = 'SEG'
  AND   "SOPClassUID"   = '1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4'
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Same check for RTSTRUCT modality (SOP class differs, so only modality filter used)
SELECT  "SOPInstanceUID",
        "Modality",
        "instance_size"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "Modality"      = 'RTSTRUCT'
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Check if any SEG objects still keep other reference columns populated
SELECT  COUNT(*) AS "seg_with_any_reference"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "Modality" = 'SEG'
  AND ( "ReferencedSeriesSequence"  IS NOT NULL
     OR "ReferencedImageSequence"   IS NOT NULL
     OR "SourceImageSequence"       IS NOT NULL
     OR "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NOT NULL );
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Byte‑sizes for each “reference‑free” SEG / RTSTRUCT object
SELECT  "collection_name",
        "StudyInstanceUID",
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        "instance_size"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   (
          ("Modality"    = 'SEG'
           AND "SOPClassUID" = '1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4')
          OR
          ("Modality"    = 'RTSTRUCT')
        )
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate sizes by collection / study / series in KILOBYTES (rounded)
SELECT  "collection_name",
        "StudyInstanceUID",
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        ROUND(SUM("instance_size")/1024,1) AS "series_kb"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   (
          ("Modality"    = 'SEG'
           AND "SOPClassUID" = '1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4')
          OR ("Modality" = 'RTSTRUCT')
        )
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
GROUP BY "collection_name",
         "StudyInstanceUID",
         "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Add viewer URL and sort largest → smallest
SELECT  "collection_name",
        "StudyInstanceUID",
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        ROUND(SUM("instance_size")/1024,1) AS "series_kb",
        'https://viewer.imaging.datacommons.cancer.gov/viewer/' || "StudyInstanceUID" AS "viewer_url"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   (
          ("Modality"    = 'SEG'
           AND "SOPClassUID" = '1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4')
          OR ("Modality" = 'RTSTRUCT')
        )
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
GROUP BY "collection_name",
         "StudyInstanceUID",
         "SeriesInstanceUID"
ORDER BY "series_kb" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Same as #9, but demonstrate HAVING clause to filter very small series (<10 KB excluded)
SELECT  "collection_name",
        "StudyInstanceUID",
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        ROUND(SUM("instance_size")/1024,1) AS "series_kb",
        'https://viewer.imaging.datacommons.cancer.gov/viewer/' || "StudyInstanceUID" AS "viewer_url"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   (
          ("Modality"    = 'SEG'
           AND "SOPClassUID" = '1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.66.4')
          OR ("Modality" = 'RTSTRUCT')
        )
  AND   "ReferencedSeriesSequence"    IS NULL
  AND   "ReferencedImageSequence"     IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageSequence"         IS NULL
  AND   "SourceImageEvidenceSequence" IS NULL
GROUP BY "collection_name",
         "StudyInstanceUID",
         "SeriesInstanceUID"
HAVING  SUM("instance_size")/1024 >= 10   -- only ≥10 KB
ORDER BY "series_kb" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These progressively walk you from basic inspection to the final aggregated answer you can further adapt (e.g., remove the LIMIT clause) when running in your Snowflake environment.
